---
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import BranchLab from '../../labs/branches/BranchLab.astro';
import '../../labs/branches/branches.css';
const captures=[
 {label:'Image handoff',file:'reference-handoff',alt:'Actual PanelForge chat composer with the fictional Sunday Studio reference attached',caption:'The actual gallery action brings the selected image into the chat composer.'},
 {label:'Original retained',file:'original-retained',alt:'Actual PanelForge original conversation after both revision branches were created',caption:'The original four-message conversation remains available after both edits and the preferred choice.'},
 {label:'Patched comparison',file:'comparison',alt:'Actual PanelForge comparison displaying the bold and quiet fictional revision branches',caption:'Both revisions render in the actual comparison view using the locally committed, unreleased API-envelope fix.'},
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Branch Lab | Change the brief, keep the work | David Blumenau" description="Follow an actual PanelForge reference handoff through preserved alternatives, comparison and a preferred branch. Replay recorded local results with fictional content and seeded answers.">
  <main id="main" class="bl-page">
    <section class="bl-hero wrap" id="top"><a class="bl-back" href="/work/panelforge/"><Icon name="arrow-left" /> The PanelForge story</a><div class="bl-hero-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Branch Lab / A creative direction worth keeping</p><h1>Change the brief.<br /><em>Keep the work.</em></h1></div><div class="bl-hero-copy"><p>A promising answer can lead in more than one direction. Trying a different brief should leave the earlier path available.</p><p>I built PanelForge's reference handoff and conversation branches to carry that shared beginning through the work.</p></div></div><div class="bl-hero-foot"><a href="#bl-title">Carry a reference <Icon name="arrow-right" /> revise <Icon name="arrow-right" /> compare</a><span>Actual app execution / fictional content / 15 October 2026</span></div></section>
    <div class="wrap"><BranchLab /></div>
    <section class="bl-film wrap" aria-labelledby="bl-film-title"><header><div><p class="eyebrow">Watch the actual app</p><h2 id="bl-film-title">The original<br /><em>really stays.</em></h2></div><p>A separate browser and a fresh local database. The real interface carries the reference, makes two forks, selects Quiet and returns to the original.</p></header><figure><video controls playsinline preload="none" poster="/media/branches/comparison.webp" aria-label="Actual PanelForge reference handoff and preserved-branch workflow" aria-describedby="bl-film-caption"><source src="/media/branches/execution.mp4" type="video/mp4" /><track kind="captions" src="/media/branches/execution.vtt" srclang="en" label="English" default />Your browser does not support this video. <a href="/media/branches/execution.mp4">Download the recording.</a></video><figcaption id="bl-film-caption">An edited screen recording of the actual isolated app, with browser loading intervals removed. Fictional Sunday Studio data and deterministic fixture answers; no model inference or image generation. The interactive exhibit above replays the observed database results.</figcaption></figure><p class="bl-patch-note"><Icon name="check" /><span>The app in this recording includes local commit <code>905cceef4</code>, an unreleased fix for the comparison view's API-envelope handling.</span></p><details><summary>Read the recording's text alternative</summary><p>A Sunday Studio poster moves from Gallery to Chat. Two initial fixture exchanges establish the original conversation. Editing the later brief creates Bold and Quiet siblings, each copying the same two-message opening and input image. The native preference endpoint selects Quiet. The patched comparison renders both revisions, and the branch tree keeps all three connected. Returning to the original shows its unchanged four messages.</p><p>The actual fork endpoints return 202; the preference update returns 200. A database snapshot from before the edits matches all original message rows afterward. Queue dispatch and inference are disabled in the fixture.</p></details></section>
    <section class="bl-captures wrap" data-branch-captures aria-labelledby="bl-captures-title"><div class="bl-captures-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Look at the working surface</p><h2 id="bl-captures-title">Three moments<br /><em>in the same workflow.</em></h2></div><div class="bl-capture-controls" role="group" aria-label="Choose an actual app capture">{captures.map((capture,i)=><button type="button" data-capture={capture.file} data-src={`/media/branches/${capture.file}.webp`} data-alt={capture.alt} data-caption={capture.caption} aria-pressed={i===0}>{capture.label}</button>)}</div></div><figure><img data-capture-image src="/media/branches/reference-handoff.webp" width="1440" height="1000" alt={captures[0].alt} loading="lazy" /><figcaption data-capture-caption>{captures[0].caption}</figcaption><a data-capture-open href="/media/branches/reference-handoff.webp" class="text-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the full-size capture <Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></a></figure><p class="bl-patch-note"><Icon name="check" /><span>Actual local app captures with fictional data and fixture answers. The comparison capture demonstrates unreleased local source <code>905cceef4</code>.</span></p></section>
    <section class="bl-context wrap"><div><p class="eyebrow">The useful part of a revision</p><h2>Keep the beginning.<br /><em>Explore the difference.</em></h2></div><div><p>The selected image has an identity in the workspace. The first exchange establishes a shared context. Editing a later message gives the new direction its own conversation, while the original remains connected.</p><p>The preference is a choice within that family. It lets one direction lead without discarding the others.</p><a href="/media/branches/receipt.json" class="text-link">Inspect the observed result <Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></a><br /><a href="/work/panelforge/" class="text-link">Read the PanelForge story <Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></a></div></section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
<script>import { initBranchCaptures } from '../../labs/branches/controller';document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-branch-captures]').forEach(initBranchCaptures);</script>
